      "content": "Media framing significantly differs by focusing on legitimacy and intent. \"Peaceful protests\" are often described with neutral or positive language, highlighting specific demands and civil rights. Conversely, \"urban riots\" are framed using charged, negative terminology emphasizing disorder, violence, and property damage. Furthermore, the demographic involved heavily influences the narrative, with media often amplifying certain groups' socioeconomic status when depicting unrest.",
