    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a really stark difference. why do you think news outlets default to those specific descriptors, like \"gang activity\" versus \"civic disruption\"? is it just about following a standard journalistic pattern, or is there a deeper reason the media characterizes certain groups' actions as inherently more threatening than others?",
